    {
      "id": 900,
      "type": "MarkdownNote",
      "pos": [
        0,
        0
      ],
      "size": [
        460,
        700
      ],
      "flags": {},
      "order": 22,
      "mode": 0,
      "color": "#222",
      "bgcolor": "#000",
      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "## LTX-2.5: Guidance Control (STG + Modality)\n\nTwo guidance patches sit between the model and the sampler and act on **different axes**:\n\n- **Spatio-Temporal Guidance (STG)** - `scale 1.5` on block `29`, active from 0% to 60% of the\n  schedule. Each step runs one extra forward pass with that block's self-attention degraded, then\n  steers away from it: sharper spatial detail and more coherent motion, no prompt changes.\n- **Modality Guidance (A/V coupling)** - `modality_scale 3.0` for the whole schedule. Runs one extra\n  pass with the audio->video and video->audio cross-attention severed and pushes the result back\n  toward the coupled prediction, so the hammer impact and its clang stay locked together.\n- **Dual CFG guider** keeps `video_cfg` and `audio_cfg` separate (both 1.0 for the distilled model).\n\nSet STG `scale` to 0 or `modality_scale` to 1.0 to switch either one off and compare. Each active\npatch adds roughly one forward pass per step, so the 8-step default costs up to ~4 passes/step.\n`LTXV Duration Predictor` is **not** used here: it needs the LTX 2.4 duration head\n(`ModelPatchLoader`), which is not part of the LTX-2.5 release."
      ],
      "widgets_values_named": {
        "text": "## LTX-2.5: Guidance Control (STG + Modality)\n\nTwo guidance patches sit between the model and the sampler and act on **different axes**:\n\n- **Spatio-Temporal Guidance (STG)** - `scale 1.5` on block `29`, active from 0% to 60% of the\n  schedule. Each step runs one extra forward pass with that block's self-attention degraded, then\n  steers away from it: sharper spatial detail and more coherent motion, no prompt changes.\n- **Modality Guidance (A/V coupling)** - `modality_scale 3.0` for the whole schedule. Runs one extra\n  pass with the audio->video and video->audio cross-attention severed and pushes the result back\n  toward the coupled prediction, so the hammer impact and its clang stay locked together.\n- **Dual CFG guider** keeps `video_cfg` and `audio_cfg` separate (both 1.0 for the distilled model).\n\nSet STG `scale` to 0 or `modality_scale` to 1.0 to switch either one off and compare. Each active\npatch adds roughly one forward pass per step, so the 8-step default costs up to ~4 passes/step.\n`LTXV Duration Predictor` is **not** used here: it needs the LTX 2.4 duration head\n(`ModelPatchLoader`), which is not part of the LTX-2.5 release."
      }
    },
